{"schema_version":"benchmark-q1-semantic-issue-coverage-judgment-luna5","question_id":"Q1-semantic-issue-coverage","status":"ok","judge_run_name":"luna8-v4-medium-196-k2-horizon-high-full200-2026-09-29","prediction_set_name":"k2-horizon-high-full200-2026-09-29","paper_id":"2509.11951","judge_input_sha256":"5347e7bd3f7fbb96b003715f2d969f3bfccb523ba120d8c505123b4600b62b61","gold_decisions":[{"gold_issue_id":"2509.11951:I001","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-002","focus_relation":"different_causal_subject","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2509.11951:I001:U001","2509.11951:I001:U002","2509.11951:I001:U003","2509.11951:I001:U004","2509.11951:I001:U005","2509.11951:I001:U006"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-002:U001","ISSUE-002:U002","ISSUE-002:U004","ISSUE-002:U007"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"ISSUE-002 diagnoses failure of the auxiliary wave's terminal support condition for a particular finite numerical row, whereas the gold issue concerns the more fundamental failure to ensure that a finite enclosing radius exists for every Lipschitz domain, including unbounded domains. Its repair does not restrict the standing domain class or establish existence of the enclosing ball.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2509.11951:I002","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-001","focus_relation":"different_operation_step_or_formula","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2509.11951:I002:U001","2509.11951:I002:U002","2509.11951:I002:U003","2509.11951:I002:U005","2509.11951:I002:U006"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-001:U001","ISSUE-001:U002","ISSUE-001:U007"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"ISSUE-001 identifies an incorrect Gaussian product and normalization factor in the pointwise reconstruction formula. It does not recognize the separate endpoint defect that the quantified p=0 case makes C_p and the proof undefined, nor does it supply C_0=1.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2509.11951:I003","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-002","focus_relation":"different_obligation_or_hypothesis","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2509.11951:I003:U001","2509.11951:I003:U002","2509.11951:I003:U003","2509.11951:I003:U004","2509.11951:I003:U005","2509.11951:I003:U006"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-002:U001","ISSUE-002:U002","ISSUE-002:U007"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"ISSUE-002 concerns a geometric terminal-support/admissibility condition for the auxiliary wave and a particular eta row. It does not identify the theorem's unbound alpha or the necessity of imposing the balanced relation alpha=delta^(2/s) for the claimed convergence rate.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2509.11951:I004","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-001","focus_relation":"different_operation_step_or_formula","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2509.11951:I004:U001","2509.11951:I004:U002","2509.11951:I004:U003","2509.11951:I004:U004","2509.11951:I004:U005","2509.11951:I004:U006"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-001:U001","ISSUE-001:U005","ISSUE-001:U007"],"same_causal_subject":true,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"ISSUE-001 addresses a normalization error in the pointwise reconstruction caused by an incorrect anisotropic Gaussian calculation. It does not recognize that the boundary waves depend on finite tau and that the reconstruction identity is only a tau-to-infinity limit with a finite-tau approximation error, not an exact finite-tau Radon equality.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]}],"audit":{"all_gold_ids_decided":true,"all_ranked_candidates_considered":true,"target_type_not_used_for_identity":true,"severity_not_used_for_identity":true,"prediction_reuse_requires_explicit_issue_support":true,"each_gold_credited_at_most_once":true,"combined_entries_are_self_contained_diagnoses":true,"support_limit_three_respected":true}}